      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1343",
      "html": "<p>Identification: body charcoal gray to black with white spots and a white band in the caudal fin. Dorsal base length to caudal depth ratio, 3.2-3.5 SL.</p><ul><li>Lateral line plates: 23-25</li><li>Dorsal plates: 6-7</li><li>Interdorsal plates: 5-7</li><li>Adipose-caudal plates: 7-8</li><li>Folded dorsal fin plates: 11-12</li><li>Postanal plates: 11-12</li></ul><p>Type locality: Río Manipitare (Río Siapa drainage), from about 5-8 kilometers upstream from confluence with Río Siapa, Depto Río Negro, Estado Amazonas, Venezuela.</p>"
